# XCU export
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The special built-in utilities are described inside
# utilities/V3_chap02.html (the page utilities/export.html only redirects
# there), so anchors name V3_chap02.html and the .cov file accounts for
# the units by hand.

assertion  XCU.export.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/set the export attribute for variables
class      required
says       export name=word sets the variable and gives it the export
           attribute, so utilities run later see it; a plain assignment does
           not export.
test       t/001-set-and-export.sh

assertion  XCU.export.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/set the export attribute for variables
class      required
says       export name gives an existing variable the export attribute, and
           later assignments to it are still passed on; a variable that was
           unset when exported is passed on once it is assigned.
test       t/002-name-only.sh

assertion  XCU.export.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/declaration utility
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.1.1
class      required
since      2024
says       The words of the form name=word given to export are expanded as
           assignments: tilde after = and after colons, no field splitting
           and no pathname expansion.
test       t/003-declaration-utility.sh

assertion  XCU.export.004
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/When <b>-p</b> is specified, <a href="#export"
class      required
says       export -p writes one line per exported variable as export
           name=value (value quoted so the line can be read back), and just
           export name for an exported variable that is unset; a variable
           that is not exported is not listed.
test       t/004-p-format.sh

assertion  XCU.export.005
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/attempt to modify a <i>readonly</i> variable using
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.1
class      required
says       Giving a new value to a read-only variable with export is an
           error: the status is non-zero (a non-interactive shell may exit)
           and the value is unchanged.
test       t/005-readonly-error.sh

assertion  XCU.export.006
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/special built-in shall support XBD
class      required
says       export accepts "--" as the end of options.
test       t/006-double-hyphen.sh
